Package: cellpacman
Title: PAinted Cell and coMpound ANalysis (PACMAN)
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Garrett", "Kinnebrew", , "garrett.kinnebrew@osumc.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Concentration-response analysis of Cell Painting morphological
    profiles. Well-level features are z-score normalized within plate,
    embedded in two dimensions with UMAP, and clustered with DBSCAN separately
    for each known compound and jointly for unknown (unannotated) wells. A
    principal curve fitted through the concentration-ordered cluster centroids
    of each known compound defines a concentration trajectory; unknown clusters
    are projected onto every trajectory to identify the most similar known
    compound and an interpolated effective concentration. Wilcoxon rank-sum
    tests with multiplicity correction identify features that change along a
    trajectory, that discriminate unknown clusters, or that separate any two
    compounds or clusters. The package has no graphical dependencies beyond
    'ggplot2' and 'plotly'; an interactive Shiny front end is distributed
    separately as the 'cellpacman-shiny' application.
